-- title:
--   Lemma A.14 — output likelihood ratio $\frac{d(\zeta K)}{d(\eta K)}(Y)=\mathbb E[g(X)\mid Y]$
-- statement:
--   Let $\zeta\ll\eta$ be probability measures, $K$ a Markov kernel, $X\sim\eta$, and let $Y$ have conditional law $K(X,\cdot)$ given $X$. Then $\zeta K\ll\eta K$, and with $g=d\zeta/d\eta$, almost surely
--   $$\frac{d(\zeta K)}{d(\eta K)}(Y)=\mathbb E[g(X)\mid Y].$$
--
--   In the forward direction of the goal it identifies the observation density $d(\nu K_t)/d(\mu K_t)$ with the posterior mean of $d\nu/d\mu$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: X ∼ η and Y with conditional law K(X, ·) → the joint law η ⊗ₘ K, with 𝔼[· | Y] the conditional expectation given σ(Y) = comap Prod.snd, and almost surely meaning η ⊗ₘ K-a.e.; reason: the statement only involves the joint law of (X, Y)
--   - encoding: unspecified spaces → arbitrary measurable spaces; reason: the paper does not fix the spaces; no space is excluded
-- source:
--   Li–Zadik, Functional inequalities from the fundamental limits of Bayesian estimation, STOC 2027 submission (held version, sha256 5ea05e95…8ed487), Lemma A.14, p.58 (PDF 58)

import Mathlib

set_option autoImplicit false

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory
open scoped ENNReal ContDiff

namespace PhiSobBayes

/-- **Lemma A.14 (output likelihood ratio).** Let `ζ ≪ η` be probability measures, `K` a Markov
kernel, `X ∼ η` and `Y` with conditional law `K(X, ·)` given `X`. Then `ζK ≪ ηK`, and with
`g = dζ/dη`, almost surely `d(ζK)/d(ηK)(Y) = 𝔼[g(X) | Y]`.

Li–Zadik, *Functional inequalities from the fundamental limits of Bayesian estimation*, STOC 2027 submission (held version, sha256 5ea05e95…8ed487), Lemma A.14, p.58 (PDF 58).

**Formalization Note** The law of `(X, Y)` is `η ⊗ₘ K`; `ζK` is `ζ.bind K`. `𝔼[g(X) | Y]` is the
conditional expectation under `η ⊗ₘ K` given the σ-algebra generated by the second coordinate, and
"almost surely" is `η ⊗ₘ K`-a.e. Densities are `Measure.rnDeriv`, read as real numbers. The spaces
are arbitrary measurable spaces. -/
theorem lemma_A_14 {α β : Type*} [MeasurableSpace α] [mβ : MeasurableSpace β]
    (ζ η : Measure α) [IsProbabilityMeasure ζ] [IsProbabilityMeasure η] (hζη : ζ ≪ η)
    (K : Kernel α β) [IsMarkovKernel K] :
    ζ.bind K ≪ η.bind K ∧
      (fun p : α × β => ((ζ.bind K).rnDeriv (η.bind K) p.2).toReal) =ᵐ[η ⊗ₘ K]
        condExp (MeasurableSpace.comap Prod.snd mβ) (η ⊗ₘ K)
          (fun p : α × β => (ζ.rnDeriv η p.1).toReal) := by sorry

end PhiSobBayes
